                <pb facs="0875" n="765" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg765"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Hirsch.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-05-13"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 13,
                        1890</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 87.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 118 of the 25th
                    ultimo, in further reference to the alleged robbery, about 1 year ago, of the
                    American missionaries Rev. Mr. McDowell and Dr. Wishard by three Nestorian
                    mountaineers, whose names are given in your note to the Sublime Porte of the
                    24th ultimo.</p>
                <p>A speedy and just disposition of this complaint seems very desirable.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
